  <bioghist id="aspace_be4b014571539e8dec90b5b01311fc71">
    <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
<p>Abraham Singer, born in Austria in 1876, is mainly known as a composer of Jewish folk and popular songs. He served as cantor of Congregation Ahavath Chesed in the Bedford-Stuyvesant neighborhood of Brooklyn, NY, in 1920 and as chair of Member Committee of the Jewish Ministers Cantors' Association of America in 1936.</p>  </bioghist>
  <processinfo id="aspace_e23c3ea8e6ee043db27d48912929191a">
    <head>Processing Information</head>
<p>Decisions regarding the arrangement, description, and physical interventions taken on this collection prior to 2026 are unknown.</p><p>In 2026, copper plates mounted to wood in Box 4 were rehoused by conservators. Original paper wrapped around plates was photocopied, with the original paper discarded per curatorial decision.</p>  </processinfo>
